</span> </a> </div> </div> </section>  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-24" style="background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--t-bg-hero), var(--t-bg)); border-top: 1px solid var(--t-border);"> <div class="absolute inset-0" style="opacity: var(--t-hero-grid-opacity); background-image: linear-gradient(var(--t-hero-grid-color) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, var(--t-hero-grid-color) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 60px 60px;"></div> <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"> <div class="max-w-3xl mb-14"> <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--t-bg-accent);">Why it&#39;s one company, not four tools</span> <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold mb-4" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">
Most vendors own one link. We own the chain.
</h2> <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">
An email problem is rarely just one problem. A spoofed domain is an authentication gap, a delivery gap, and a routing gap at the same time. Point tools hand you a report and send you off to find someone who can act on it. We diagnose it, fix the records, send the mail, and route what comes back. One company, one SLA, one expert who stays on it until it's solved.
</p> </div> <!-- Four-link chain --> <div class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row items-stretch gap-4 lg:gap-0">  <div class="flex-1 rounded-2xl p-6" style="background: var(--t-card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border); border-top: 3px solid var(--color-brand-purple);"> <div class="text-xs font-bold tracking-widest mb-3" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #5751cd;">01</div> <div class="text-xl font-extrabold mb-1.5" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">Authenticate</div> <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">Prove the mail is really yours.</p> </div> <div class="flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 lg:px-2" aria-hidden="true"> <span class="text-2xl font-bold rotate-90 lg:rotate-0 inline-block" style="color: var(--t-text-muted);">&rarr;</span> </div> <div class="flex-1 rounded-2xl p-6" style="background: var(--t-card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border); border-top: 3px solid var(--color-brand-purple-light);"> <div class="text-xs font-bold tracking-widest mb-3" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #5751cd;">02</div> <div class="text-xl font-extrabold mb-1.5" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">Protect</div> <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">Stop what should never reach the inbox.</p> </div> <div class="flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 lg:px-2" aria-hidden="true"> <span class="text-2xl font-bold rotate-90 lg:rotate-0 inline-block" style="color: var(--t-text-muted);">&rarr;</span> </div> <div class="flex-1 rounded-2xl p-6" style="background: var(--t-card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border); border-top: 3px solid var(--color-brand-cyan);"> <div class="text-xs font-bold tracking-widest mb-3" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #0e7490;">03</div> <div class="text-xl font-extrabold mb-1.5" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">Deliver</div> <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">Get the good mail actually delivered.</p> </div> <div class="flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 lg:px-2" aria-hidden="true"> <span class="text-2xl font-bold rotate-90 lg:rotate-0 inline-block" style="color: var(--t-text-muted);">&rarr;</span> </div> <div class="flex-1 rounded-2xl p-6" style="background: var(--t-card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border); border-top: 3px solid #4ec1cd;"> <div class="text-xs font-bold tracking-widest mb-3" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: #0e7490;">04</div> <div class="text-xl font-extrabold mb-1.5" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">Route</div> <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">Send what is left where it belongs.</p> </div>  </div> <p class="mt-10 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">
No other email vendor owns all four links. That isn't a slogan. It's why the problems nobody else could untangle tend to end up here, and why fixing one of them almost always surfaces the next.
</p> </div> </section>  <section class="py-24" style="background: var(--t-bg-subtle); border-top: 1px solid var(--t-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--t-border);"> <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"> <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12"> <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--t-bg-accent);">The math</span> <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold mb-4" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">
About 90% of the capability. About half the price.
</h2> <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">
The pattern holds across every category we compete in: enterprise security, DMARC reporting, transactional sending, cold outreach. We give you the capability that actually moves your email program. When you genuinely need the other 10%, we will tell you, and we will point you somewhere better.
</p> </div> <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4"> <a href="/resources/proofpoint-alternatives/" class="block rounded-xl p-5 transition-all duration-200" style="background: var(--t-card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border); text-decoration: none;"> <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--t-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono);">vs. Proofpoint</div> <div class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">Phishing Protection</div> <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">Click-time URL inspection, BEC defense, impersonation. Half the price, no procurement gauntlet.</p> <span class="text-sm font-semibold" style="color: var(--t-bg-accent);">Compare &rarr;</span> </a><a href="/resources/easydmarc-alternatives/" class="block rounded-xl p-5 transition-all duration-200" style="background: var(--t-card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border); text-decoration: none;"> <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--t-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono);">vs. EasyDMARC</div> <div class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">DMARC Report</div> <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">Multi-region G2 Category Leader. Free tier for one domain. Volume-based pricing.</p> <span class="text-sm font-semibold" style="color: var(--t-bg-accent);">Compare &rarr;</span> </a><a href="/resources/sendgrid-alternatives/" class="block rounded-xl p-5 transition-all duration-200" style="background: var(--t-card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border); text-decoration: none;"> <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--t-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono);">vs. SendGrid</div> <div class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">Outbound SMTP</div> <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">Operating since 2014. Free up to 1,000 emails per month, no credit card.</p> <span class="text-sm font-semibold" style="color: var(--t-bg-accent);">Compare &rarr;</span> </a><a href="/resources/smartlead-alternatives/" class="block rounded-xl p-5 transition-all duration-200" style="background: var(--t-card-bg); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border); text-decoration: none;"> <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold mb-2" style="color: var(--t-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono);">vs. Smartlead</div> <div class="text-lg font-bold mb-2" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">NuReply</div> <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">Bring your own mailbox cold outreach. Built-in deliverability hygiene.</p> <span class="text-sm font-semibold" style="color: var(--t-bg-accent);">Compare &rarr;</span> </a> </div> <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-center" style="color: var(--t-text-muted);">
See the full set on <a href="/compare/" style="color: var(--t-bg-accent); font-weight: 600;">our comparisons page</a>.
</p> </div> </section>  <section class="py-20" style="background: var(--t-bg-subtle); border-top: 1px solid var(--t-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--t-border);"> <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"> <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--t-bg-accent);">How customers find us</span> <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold mb-6" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">
One product brings them in. The rest of the portfolio keeps them.
</h2> <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);"> <p>
A team comes to AutoSPF to fix an SPF record that's blowing the 10-DNS-lookup limit. The immediate problem gets fixed. A few weeks later they realize the bigger issue isn't SPF flattening, it's that their domain has no DMARC enforcement and they don't actually know who's sending mail as them. So they add DMARC Report alongside AutoSPF, and finally see the full picture.
</p> <p>
A business signs up for Outbound SMTP's free tier because their office copiers stopped authenticating to Office 365 and can no longer send scan-to-email. The copiers come back online. A few weeks in, the IT team notices that the mail our relay is putting out actually shows up properly SPF and DKIM aligned. They ask what else we can help with. Turns out they've had a long-running email-deliverability problem nobody else has been able to fix. We work that one next.
</p> <p>
A Phishing Protection customer keeps catching the same impersonation pattern at the gateway and asks why the bad mail keeps coming. The answer is upstream: their DMARC posture is at <code>p=none</code> (anyone can spoof their domain at will) and their SPF is at <code>~all</code> (softfail, so even authenticated mail isn't strictly enforced). They add DMARC Report to push toward enforcement, the impersonation rate drops, and the expert running the rollout is the same one who's been answering their support tickets for years.
</p> <p>
The portfolio looks deliberate now because it is, just not top-down deliberate. Every product is a yes to a customer who couldn't get one elsewhere. The shape only becomes visible looking back.
</p> <p> <a href="/about-us/" style="color: var(--t-bg-accent); font-weight: 600;">Read the full story &rarr;</a> </p> </div> </div> </section>  <section class="py-20" style="background: var(--t-bg);"> <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8"> <div class="rounded-2xl p-10" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--t-card-bg), var(--t-bg-subtle)); border: 1px solid var(--t-card-border);"> <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--t-bg-accent);">In the customer&#39;s words</span> <blockquote class="mt-6 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold leading-snug" style="font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--t-text);">
&ldquo;DuoCircle is easy to work with and willing to make it happen. Their solution is solid.&rdquo;
</blockquote> <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4"> <div> <div class="font-semibold" style="color: var(--t-text);">Dennis Schroder</div> <div class="text-sm" style="color: var(--t-text-secondary);">President and CEO, Arak&yuml;ta</div> </div> <a href="/case-study/arakyta-case-study/" class="inline-flex items-center font-semibold text-sm" style="color: var(--t-bg-accent);">
